1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Culiacán reaches 45 °C.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:12,000
If you're 72 and don't have a car,
how far is the nearest cool place, on foot?

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
This is Refugio. Each hexagon
is roughly one city block.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Its color says how many minutes you walk, along the real
streets at a slow pace, to an air-conditioned place
where you can stay without buying anything.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
In Culiacán, 17,441 older adults live
more than 15 minutes away.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Let's search from a home
in colonia Libertad.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Amazon Location turns the address into a point and,
at the same time, draws how far I get on foot
in 5, 10 and 15 minutes...

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,000
...and the walking route to the nearest refuge:
the science museum, 26 minutes away.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:05,000
My open-data map says the same: 26.
Not even the 15-minute area reaches it.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Counting pharmacies and stores, where you step in
to buy water, almost everyone is close.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
This filter keeps only the places
where older adults live.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The list of areas shows
where refuges are missing.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:35,000
And these are ten public schools that, opened as refuges,
would take older adults within 10 minutes
from 40.7 to 51.4 percent.

14
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:45,000
And the same pipeline runs
in Hermosillo and Mexicali.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
How does it work? The data comes from the
Registry of Open Data on AWS, in Amazon S3:
places and streets from Overture Maps...

16
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,000
...and the population aged 60 or more from Meta.
I only read each city's area:
Culiacán downloads in 34 seconds.

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:10,000
With 57,000 street segments I build a walking network
and compute the minutes for every hexagon.

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The site is static, on AWS Amplify, and the personal
search calls Amazon Location: maps, places and routes.

19
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Is it reliable? I compared 50 random points
with Amazon Location's walking routes:

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
the median difference is half a minute,
and 94% are within 2 minutes.

21
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Where Overture lacks a place, Amazon Location sometimes
has it, so the headline figure is an upper bound.

22
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Next: an official refuge network with the city.
Try it at this address.
